# What I Learned

* OSPF is a dynamic routing protocol that allows routers to automatically learn routes to remote networks.
* OSPF neighbors must establish an adjacency before routing information can be exchanged.
* OSPF Area 0 is the backbone area and was used for this single-area lab.
* `show ip route` can be used to identify routes learned through OSPF.
* `show ip ospf neighbor` can be used to verify OSPF adjacencies.
* `show ip interface brief` is useful for quickly identifying interface problems.
* A routing configuration can be correct while connectivity still fails because of a lower-layer problem.
* Physical/link connectivity should be verified before troubleshooting routing protocols.
* The redundant topology provides multiple potential paths between portions of the network.

